  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 1; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. The number of students on campus doubles at the end of every month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The original population is 12 students.\n\nIf the population doubles:\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n24-12=12\n\\]\n\nPercentage increase relative to the original population:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\%=100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. There are 10 students on campus at the beginning of the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The original population is 10 students.\n\nAfter doubling:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nThus, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the student population is multiplied by 2 after each completed month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The initial population is \\(10\\) students.\n\nAfter one completed month, the population is multiplied by \\(2\\):\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nRelative to the original population, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many students will be on campus after three completed months?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The population starts at \\(10\\) students and doubles after each completed month:\n\n- After 1 month: \\(10 \\times 2 = 20\\)\n- After 2 months: \\(20 \\times 2 = 40\\)\n- After 3 months: \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n\nEquivalently,\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^3 = 80\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: A doubling means the new population is twice the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Yes. A doubling means the population becomes twice its value at the start of that month:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^3 = 80\n\\]\n\nSo after three completed months, there will be\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many additional students would have joined campus by the end of May beyond the students present at the beginning of the year? One more thing you should know: the question concerns the number of students on campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "There are 5 completed months from the beginning of the year through the end of May. Since the population doubles each month:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^5 = 320\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 320 students on campus by the end of May. The number of additional students beyond the original 10 is:\n\n\\[\n320-10=310\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{310\\text{ additional students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
